{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/yorkshire-pilot-buried-in-france-on-86th-anniversary-of-his-death","content_id":"63ee2a9c-40c9-4774-b6e2-aae0131e7729","description":"Members of the public gathered in France yesterday (19 May 2026) to witness the burial with full military honours of a World War Two Hurricane Pilot. Squadron Leader (Sqn Ldr) George Morley Fidler was laid to rest exactly 86 years after he was lost.  ","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p><abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler joined the Royal Air Force (<abbr title=\"Royal Air Force\">RAF</abbr>) in 1934 and spent several years in Egypt, with brief spells in Cyprus and India. He was described as an ‘exceptional’ pilot by his superiors and in February 1940, he joined 607 Squadron. On the afternoon of 19 May 1940, as Hurricanes from 607 Squadron were patrolling the skies above Cambrai. <abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler’s plane was shot down.  </p>\n\n<p>Initially, <abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler’s remains were believed to have been recovered and buried in the French village of Bachy. However, in 2005 metal detectorists discovered wreckage 35km away in Oisy-le-Verger one piece of which had a serial number ‘P3535’, suggesting it came from his Hurricane. </p>\n\n<p>This prompted the Ministry of Defence (<abbr title=\"Ministry of Defence\">MOD</abbr>) to investigate the grave in Bachy to determine if it was really that of <abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler. It was soon discovered that authorities at the time had failed to consider the loss of two <abbr title=\"Royal Air Force\">RAF</abbr> Sergeants who died on the same day meaning they could not be certain it was <abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler who had been buried there. So, the headstone in Bachy was changed: the name was removed and replaced with ‘unknown Airman’. <abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler’s name was then added to the memorial to the missing.  </p>\n\n<p>However, his story did not end there. In 2022, work on the Seine-Nord Canal at Oisy-le-Verger in northern France, unearthed a Hurricane with the pilot still inside near to where Sqn Leader Fidler’s aircraft was last seen. DNA testing then proved this pilot was Sqn Leader Fidler.  </p>\n\n<p>Today’s service was organised by the <abbr title=\"Ministry of Defence\">MOD</abbr>’s Joint Casualty and Compassionate Centre (<abbr title=\"Joint Casualty &amp; Compassionate Centre\">JCCC</abbr>), also known as the ‘<abbr title=\"Ministry of Defence\">MOD</abbr> War Detectives’ who work to identify the recovered remains of British military casualties. </p>\n\n<figure class=\"image embedded\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d5017fcae986635db923b/s960_Photo_3_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg\" alt=\"\"></div>\n<figcaption><p>The bearer party, comprised of serving personnel from RAF Halton, carry Squadron Leader Fidler’s coffin (Crown Copyright)</p></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Nicola Nash, <abbr title=\"Ministry of Defence\">MOD</abbr> War Detective said: </p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p class=\"last-child\"><abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler has been buried today 86 years after he was killed. His story has been known to us since his grave was ‘unnamed’ many years ago. It has been wonderful to finally find him and be able to put him to rest. Today we honour him and the sacrifices he made all those years ago.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>The service took place at Commonwealth War Graves Commission (<abbr title=\"Commonwealth War Graves Commission\">CWGC</abbr>) London Cemetery and Extension, France.  </p>\n\n<figure class=\"image embedded\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4fd3fcae986635db9238/s960_Photo_2-_Members_of_RAF_Halton__607_Squadron_and_a_Trumpeter_of_the_Band_of_the_Royal_Air_Force_College_stand_behind_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_headstone..jpg\" alt=\"\"></div>\n<figcaption><p>Members of RAF Halton, 607 Squadron and a Trumpeter of the Band of the Royal Air Force College stand behind Squadron Leader Fidler’s headstone (Crown Copyright)</p></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Dr James Wallis, Head of Commemorations at the <abbr title=\"Commonwealth War Graves Commission\">CWGC</abbr>, said: </p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p class=\"last-child\">It is an honour for the Commission to pay our respects to <abbr title=\"Squadron Leader\">Sqn Ldr</abbr> Fidler, following the 2022 discovery of his Hurricane along the route of the future Canal Seine-Nord Europe. That another commemorative service will be held today at his local church - in Great Ayton, Yorkshire - shows the power and impact of his war experience eight decades on. Now resting amongst fellow airmen at London Cemetery and Extension, Longueval, his grave will be cared for in perpetuity.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:37:51Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12"],"images":[{"caption":"The bearer party, composed of serving personnel from RAF Halton, carry Sqn Ldr Fidler to the graveside (Crown Copyright)","content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4f6ffcae986635db9233/s216_Photo_4_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4f6f229555d0fe8268bf/s300_Photo_4_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4f6fc75cc34a8ff8f5a1/s465_Photo_4_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4f6f279ebb7d24f8f53a/s630_Photo_4_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4f6ffcae986635db9234/s712_Photo_4_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a0d4f6f279ebb7d24f8f539/s960_Photo_4_-_The_bearer_party__comprised_of_serving_personnel_from_RAF_Halton__carry_Squadron_Leader_Fidler_s_coffin..jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"news_story","first_published_at":"2026-05-20T09:37:51+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/yorkshire-pilot-buried-in-france-on-86th-anniversary-of-his-death","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/yorkshire-pilot-buried-in-france-on-86th-anniversary-of-his-death","base_path":"/government/news/yorkshire-pilot-buried-in-france-on-86th-anniversary-of-his-death","content_id":"63ee2a9c-40c9-4774-b6e2-aae0131e7729","document_type":"news_story","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-05-20T08:37:51Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Yorkshire pilot buried in France on 86th anniversary of his death","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/yorkshire-pilot-buried-in-france-on-86th-anniversary-of-his-death","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","details":{"acronym":"MOD","brand":"ministry-of-defence","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960